// way every other tolerance in this project was: from the measured drift, with
// a negative control pinning the other side.
//
// The scalar kernels are fp32 throughout and stay inside the 2e-4 every stage
// shares. The WMMA path narrows q, k, v and the softmax weights to fp16 --
// which is not a choice, it is the only operand type this device's matrix
// cores take -- and fp16 carries 11 bits of mantissa, so 4.9e-4 of relative
// error per rounded input. Against the diffusers reference at 320 tokens the
// whole stack measures 2.4e-3 of its RMS; the bound is 5e-3, which is a little
// over twice that and still 260x below where the controls in
// TestGPUWMMANegativeControls land.
//
// Worth being explicit about what this is not: it is not a claim that fp16
// attention is as accurate as fp32 attention. It is a claim that the error is
// the one fp16 rounding predicts and not a bug, and that it is two to three
// orders of magnitude below every way of getting the kernel wrong that has
// been tried. Stage 2 found fp16 could not hold the VAE's intermediates at
// all (scores of 1.16e7 against a 65504 limit); attention's softmax weights
// are bounded by 1 by construction, which is why the same narrowing is safe
// here and was not there.
const fp16RelTol = 5e-3

// tolFor is the bound a given kernel is held to.
func tolFor(k Kernel) float64 {
	if k == KernelSimple || k == KernelFlash {
		return relTol
	}
	return fp16RelTol
}

